{
  "about": "The genex facade's agent-facing vocabularies, held by native/genex-rust/crates/genex/tests/vocabulary.rs (RUNTIME_KEYS, InstallErrorCode, the gpu_pass registration code, the Level-2 calls, which call each [[wgsl]] kind feeds, and the frame calls temporal effects need: draw ids and camera cuts; the environment calls with the wire spellings of its kinds and of `HdriSun`; the local-light and emissive calls of RQ6; the look's fog calls, A.5's volumetric opt-out among them; the calls that build a world's look: reflection probes and irradiance volumes, decals, grading and white balance, the lens, the night sky and subsurface) and read by tests/conformance/rust-template-docs.test.ts, which checks the template docs name each. Change both sides with this file. Its `meshlets` block is the renderer's `genex_meshlets` glTF extras schema (genex-render's meshlet.rs, the host's src/shared/render-quality.ts), held by vocabulary.rs and tests/conformance/genex-toml.test.ts. Its `animation`, `stream`, `nav`, `assets` and `lod` blocks are the game systems' calls and refusals, empty until each area pins what works (`assets` is pinned: SF-1a's sim-side reads; `animation` holds the rig importer's and the graph builder's refusals; `stream` holds the cell grid's; `nav` holds the bake input's, the tile bake's and the off-mesh links' refusals and `frame.lines`). Its `textures` block is the importer's `genex_textures` GLB extras schema (glb-textures.ts), held by tests/conformance/genex-toml.test.ts; C-14 pins the Rust reader against it in vocabulary.rs. Its `runtimeRender` block is __render's display-only texture facts (C-11): the keys, the family spellings and the asset issue codes.",
  "runtimeKeys": [
    "version",
    "contractVersion",
    "seed",
    "frame",
    "simulatedMs",
    "running",
    "fps",
    "held",
    "pointerLock",
    "hud",
    "camera",
    "error",
    "player",
    "volatile",
    "__render",
    "__stream",
    "assets",
    "checksum"
  ],
